  Solar: "Solar Exclusion Tax Relief",
  theinitial: "The initial purchaser of a building with an active solar energy system may qualify for an exclusion from assessment on that portion of the value attributable to an active solar energy system, less the amount of any rebates. To qualify for this exclusion, an Initial Purchaser Claim for Solar Energy System New Construction Exclusion must be filed with this office.",
  theaddition: "The addition of an active solar energy system to an existing property is automatically excluded from assessment. For example, the installation of photovoltaic (PV) cells on an existing home would not be subject to assessment. There is no need to file an exclusion form to benefit from this exclusion.",
  Note: "Note: ",
  anactive: "an \u201Cactive solar energy system\u201D does not include solar water heating for swimming pools or hot tubs.",
  InitialPurchaserButton: "Initial Purchases Claim for Solar Energy System New Construction Exclusions",
  Seismic: "Seismic Exclusion Tax Relief",
  Theseismic: "The Seismic Exclusion allows tax exclusion from new construction that includes construction of seismic retrofitting improvements or other improvements that utilize earthquake hazard mitigation technologies on an existing building. The exclusion only applies to existing portion of the buildings. Additions that did not exist prior to the seismic construction would not qualify for the exclusion. Construction of entirely new buildings would also not qualify for this exclusion. ",
  Theexclusion: "The exclusion does not include other alterations, such as new plumbing, electrical or other added finishing materials, completed during seismic related work. "
